ild position its output is wrapped in\n`<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->` and plain strings it returns are escaped there,\nsince they never passed through `html`. Non-empty component children\nget the same marker pair before `render` sees them. Function-valued\n`on*` props are dropped. Static pages must stay byte-identical, which\n`test/ssr.ts` asserts with exact strings.\n\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -qm \"Server handling of reactive holes in the templater\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vvej8UvWu4cWGtKVu4yRxS","type":"tool_result","content":"4848f9f Server handling of reactive holes in the templater","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"790607dd-315a-47bd-b29e-8fabdd04dba6","uuid":"43b5dcda-74d6-407b-88e7-9cd8b6522c71","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:56:14.706Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"4848f9f Server handling of reactive holes in the templater","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.unidirectional-hydration-04-server-reactive-holes/AGENTS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":57,"oldLines":6,"newStart":57,"newLines":14,"lines":[" `string | Markup`; the static `render` still returns a string."," `builders.ts` imports `Markup` as a type only, so core stays htm-free."," ","+On the server, any function in a hole (signals are callable) is","+evaluated once; in child position its output is wrapped in","+`<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->` and plain strings it returns are escaped there,","+since they never passed through `html`. Non-empty component children","+get the same marker pair before `render` sees them. Function-valued","+`on*` props are dropped. Static pages must stay byte-identical, which","+`test/ssr.ts` asserts with exact strings.","+"," When adding the `html` entry to the build, update all three esbuild"," scripts (`build-cjs`, `build-esm`, `build-esm:min`) in package.json."," The `.size-limit.js` file needs a second entry for `dist/htm.min.js`."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/nick/code/microtags.unidirectional-hydration-04-server-reactive-holes/AGENTS.md"]}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi6qDEuRhxc6koRCnkw4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] A signal in child position renders its current value between one `<!--[-->` and one `<!--]-->`\n[x] A function in child position is called once and its result is wrapped the same way, including when it returns markup, an array, `null`, or `false`\n[x] A signal or function as an attribute on a plain element renders its evaluated value; `false`, `null`, or `undefined` omits the attribute\n[x] A signal as a declared component prop reaches the render function as its plain value\n[x] Children passed to a component arrive wrapped in one marker pair; a component that drops its children emits no markers\n[x] A function-valued `on<event>` prop does not appear in the output\n[x] A page with no reactive holes and no component children is byte-identical to its output before this ticket\n[x] All Node suites and `npm test` pass\n\nTicket 04 is done, in one commit (`4848f9f`).\n\nThe server templater now handles reactive holes. All the changes are in `src/htm.ts`:\n\n1. Signals in this library are plain callable functions, so any function in a hole is called once.\n2. A function in child position has its output wrapped in `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->`. Plain strings it returns are escaped, because they never went through `html`.\n3. When a component is given children, they reach `render` wrapped in the same marker pair. With no children, nothing changes.\n4. A function-valued `on*` prop is left out of the output, on plain elements and on hosts.\n\nSeven new tests in `test/ssr.ts` check the exact output strings, including one showing that a page with no reactive holes renders the same bytes as before. No existing test expectations needed to change, because the old children tests check structure rather than exact strings.\n\nTest results: SSR 79 passing, `npm test` 195, hydration 33, hydration-dev 17, plugins 17, and build and CLI also pass. `npm run lint` still reports 2 unused-variable errors in `test/plugins.ts`. They were already there before this ticket, so I left them alone.\n\nA few other things to know:\n- The ticket asked for a commit after each checklist item. I made one commit instead, because all the items came from the same small change.\n- I added a note on the server's reactive-hole rules to `AGENTS.md`.\n- I ran `npm install` because `node_modules` was missing, and deleted `example-hydration/build/` so lint would run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":525,"cache_read_input_tokens":58374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":525},"output_tokens":662,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"790607dd-315a-47bd-b29e-8fabdd04dba6","uuid":"5de2eecd-5b2b-408a-bd21-25a9660d740a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:56:21.841Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi6qCfBiKSmjLmdD4pYn"}
